{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"init","kind":"keyword"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"sign","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Sign","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL7MXLClefV4SignO","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLClef\/Sign"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"line","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLStaffLinePosition","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLStaffLinePosition","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL20MXLStaffLinePositionV"},{"text":"? = nil, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"octaveChange","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLOctaveChange","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLOctaveChange","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL15MXLOctaveChangeV"},{"kind":"text","text":"? = nil)"}],"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"parameters","parameters":[{"name":"sign","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The sign element represents the clef symbol.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"name":"line","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Line numbers are counted from the bottom of the staff. They are only needed with the G, F, and C signs in order to position a pitch correctly on the staff. Standard values are 2 for the G sign (treble clef), 4 for the F sign (bass clef), and 3 for the C sign (alto clef). Line values can be used to specify positions outside the staff, such as a C clef positioned in the middle of a grand staff.","type":"text"}]}]},{"name":"octaveChange","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The clef-octave-change element is used for transposing clefs. A treble clef for tenors would have a value of -1."}]}]}]}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Creates a new "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MXLClef.Content"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlclef\/content-swift.struct\/init(sign:line:octavechange:)"]}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLClef","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLClef\/Content-swift.struct"]]},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLClef\/Content-swift.struct\/init(sign:line:octaveChange:)","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"init"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"sign","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL7MXLClefV4SignO","text":"Sign","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"line","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL20MXLStaffLinePositionV","text":"MXLStaffLinePosition","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"octaveChange","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL15MXLOctaveChangeV","text":"MXLOctaveChange","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?)","kind":"text"}],"roleHeading":"Initializer","externalID":"s:7IvorMXL7MXLClefV7ContentV4sign4line12octaveChangeAeC4SignO_AA20MXLStaffLinePositionVSgAA09MXLOctaveH0VSgtcfc","role":"symbol","title":"init(sign:line:octaveChange:)","symbolKind":"init"},"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter."}],"title":"IvorMXL","kind":"symbol","role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLClef/Sign":{"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLClef\/Sign","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlclef\/sign","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Sign","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"MXLClef.Sign","fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Sign","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The clef-sign type represents the different clef symbols. The jianpu sign indicates that the music that"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"follows should be in jianpu numbered notation, just as the TAB sign indicates that the music that follows"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"should be in tablature notation. Unlike TAB, a jianpu sign does not correspond to a visual clef notation."}],"role":"symbol"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLOctaveChange":{"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLOctaveChange","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLOctaveChange","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxloctavechange","role":"symbol","title":"MXLOctaveChange","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLOctaveChange","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The number of octaves to shift a pitch or clef, such as when transposing a written pitch to a sounding pitch"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(the octave-change element) or positioning a treble clef for tenors, which would use a value of -1 (the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"clef-octave-change element)."}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLClef/Content-swift.struct":{"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlclef\/content-swift.struct","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Clefs are represented by a combination of sign, line, and clef-octave-change elements."}],"title":"MXLClef.Content","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Content"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Content"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLClef\/Content-swift.struct","kind":"symbol","type":"topic"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLStaffLinePosition":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The staff-line-position type indicates the line position on a given staff. Staff lines are numbered from"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"bottom to top, with 1 being the bottom line on a staff. A staff-line-position value can extend beyond the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"range of the lines on the current staff."}],"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLStaffLinePosition"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLStaffLinePosition"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLStaffLinePosition","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlstafflineposition","title":"MXLStaffLinePosition"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLClef":{"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlclef","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Clefs are represented by a combination of sign, line, and clef-octave-change elements. The optional number"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"attribute refers to staff numbers within the part. A value of 1 is assumed if not present."}],"title":"MXLClef","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLClef"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLClef"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLClef","kind":"symbol","type":"topic"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLClef/Content-swift.struct/init(sign:line:octaveChange:)":{"kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"init","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"sign","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Sign","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL7MXLClefV4SignO","kind":"type